check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.0969145Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1115350Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1134335Z ^[[0m
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1134827Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1135401Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1135595Z 
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1135777Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1136160Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1136429Z 
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1136603Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1137183Z    if you are ready to continue.
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1137360Z 
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1137711Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1138365Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1138862Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1139185Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1139401Z 
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1139635Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1139993Z 
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1140254Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1140766Z    can use Nix.
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1140944Z 
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1141094Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1141305Z 
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1141684Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1142311Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1158739Z 
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1158890Z I will:
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1159082Z 
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1159240Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1159633Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1160018Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1160379Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1160645Z  - install Nix in to /nix
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1160916Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1161259Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1161644Z    /root
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1184290Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1184723Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1207075Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1207513Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1207733Z 
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1211140Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1211603Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1240268Z 
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1240878Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1260523Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1260995Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1261337Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1261509Z 
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1261660Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1261882Z 
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1262059Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1262406Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1262590Z 
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1262694Z If you would like to
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1262922Z see the output, try like this:
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1263071Z 
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1263218Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1263541Z   $ sh ./install-nix
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1263895Z 
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1264301Z 
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1264861Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1284060Z ^[[0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
check-code-format	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-24T17:16:13.1284558Z been installed on this system.
